# KRONOS R10 least-privilege egress-guard sudoers policy (TEMPLATE — NOT installed by this repo).
#
# A human installs this, root-owned, as /etc/sudoers.d/kronos-cybergym-egress (mode 0440),
# AFTER replacing RUNUSER with the unprivileged account that runs the CyberGym evaluation,
# AFTER installing the helper root-owned at /usr/local/sbin/kronos-cybergym-egress, and AFTER
# writing the pinned config /etc/kronos-cybergym/egress.conf (see the install runbook).
# Validate with: visudo -cf /etc/sudoers.d/kronos-cybergym-egress
#
# This grants RUNUSER password-less sudo for ONLY the three fixed, ARGUMENT-FREE verbs of the
# ONE fixed, root-owned helper path. NO wildcard: sudoers matches the command line exactly, so
# any extra argument is denied. It grants nothing else: no shell, no editor, no other binary, no
# raw iptables. The helper takes subnet/gateway/network only from the pinned root-owned
# /etc/kronos-cybergym/egress.conf and re-validates it. Never whitelist the repo's writable
# scripts/kronos-cybergym-egress — only the installed, root-owned absolute path below.

RUNUSER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/kronos-cybergym-egress apply, /usr/local/sbin/kronos-cybergym-egress remove, /usr/local/sbin/kronos-cybergym-egress status
